  "text": "\r\n\t\t Elections | Londonderry, NH \r\n Skip to Main Content \r\nCreate a Website Account   - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.    \r\nWebsite Sign In \r\n     Your Government   \t\t\t \n     Our Community   \t\t\t \n     Doing Business   \t\t\t \n     Watch   \t\t\t \n     How Do I...   \t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t Search \n\t\t\t Absentee Ballots \r\n\t\t\t Election Results \r\n\t\t\t Elections \r\n\t\t\t Filing for Office \r\n\t\t\t Voter Registration \r\nHome \nYour Government \nDepartments \nTown Clerk / Tax Collector \nVoting & Elections \nElections \r\nElections\t\t \r\n2026 State General Election \nTuesday, November 3, 2026 \n6 a.m. to 8 p.m. \nLHS Gymnasium \nPlanning to vote?  Please take a moment to review  New Hampshire’s voter identification requirements (PDF)  before Election Day. The State’s Voter ID Law explains which forms of photo identification are accepted and the process available to registered voters who do not have valid photo identification when they arrive to vote. \r\nComplimentary Transportation to the Polls for Londonderry Seniors \nThe Londonderry Senior Center will provide transportation for seniors wishing to vote in the State General Election on Tuesday, November 3, 2026. Transportation will be available from the Londonderry Senior Center, located at 535 Mammoth Road, with departures scheduled for  11:30 a.m. and 1:30 p.m. \nThe van will bring participants directly to the entrance of the Londonderry High School Gymnasium and return them to the Senior Center after voting. \nInterested in reserving a ride?  Please sign up at the Londonderry Senior Center's front desk or call  603-432-8554 . \r\nSample Ballot \nPlease note:  The  sample ballot (PDF)  is two-sided. Be sure to review both pages. \nConstitutional Questions on the Ballot \nThe November 3, 2026 ballot includes questions regarding proposed amendments to the New Hampshire Constitution. \nResidents seeking additional information or clarification regarding these questions are encouraged to visit  www.sos.nh.gov  and refer to the “Happening Now” section for additional details. \nElection Officials \r\n\t\t\t\t\tJonathan Kipp\r\nTown Moderator \r\nEmail Jonathan Kipp  \r\nTerm Expires March 2027 \r\n\t\t\t\t\tSherry Farrell\r\nTown Clerk \r\nEmail Sherry Farrell  \r\nTerm Ending March 2027 \r\n\t\t\t\t\tKristin Grages\r\nChair, Supervisors of the Checklist \r\nEmail Kristin Grages  \r\nTerm Ending March 2028 \r\n\t\t\t\t\tJohn Ambrose\r\nSupervisors of the Checklist \r\nEmail John Ambrose  \r\nTerm Ending March 2032 \r\n\t\t\t\t\tJoseph Stelmach\r\nSupervisors of the Checklist \r\nEmail Joseph Stelmach  \r\nTerm Expires March 2027 \r\n\t\t\t Agendas & Minutes \r\n\t\t\t Town Documents \r\n\t\t\t Notify Me \r\n\t\t\t Voting & Elections \r\n\t\t\t Trash & Recycling \r\n\t\t\t Town Maps \r\nContact Us \r\nTown of Londonderry \r\n268B Mammoth Road \r\nLondonderry, NH 03053 \r\nPhone:  (603) 432-1100 \r\nQuick Links \r\n         Community Events \n         Community News \n         FAQs \n         Online Services \n         Trash & Recycling \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\nSite Links \r\n         Home \n         Site Map \n         Contact Us \n         Accessibility \n         Copyright Notices \n         Privacy Policy \n/QuickLinks.aspx \r\n   Government Websites by  CivicPlus® \nLoading \r\n\t\t\t\tLoading\r\n\t\t\t Do Not Show Again \r\n\t\t\t Close \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Left \r\n\t\t\t Arrow Right \r\n[] \r\n                     Slideshow Left Arrow \r\n                     Slideshow Right Arrow \r\n ",
